From b1f0000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: do Rego Lemos, Italo <Italo.doRegoLemos@windriver.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not extend session on AJAX requests

SESSION_TIMEOUT is meant to act as an idle timeout, refreshing the
session expiry on user activity when SESSION_REFRESH is True. However
the expiry refresh in HorizonMiddleware._process_request ran before the
is_ajax() early-return, so background AJAX polling from auto-refreshing
panels (e.g. Admin > Inventory > Hosts, which polls roughly every 5s)
reset the session expiry continuously. As a result an idle but open
dashboard was never logged out and SESSION_TIMEOUT had no effect for
both keystone and OIDC/WebSSO authenticated sessions.

Move the is_ajax() check ahead of the SESSION_REFRESH block so that
only genuine (non-AJAX) user activity refreshes the session expiry.
AJAX requests no longer extend the session, making SESSION_TIMEOUT a
true idle timeout while active users remain logged in.

Signed-off-by: do Rego Lemos, Italo <Italo.doRegoLemos@windriver.com>
---
 horizon/middleware/base.py | 20 +++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/horizon/middleware/base.py b/horizon/middleware/base.py
--- a/horizon/middleware/base.py
+++ b/horizon/middleware/base.py
@@ -67,15 +67,11 @@ class HorizonMiddleware(object):
             # to avoid creating too many sessions
             return None
 
-        # Since we know the user is present and authenticated, lets refresh the
-        # session expiry if configured to do so.
-        if settings.SESSION_REFRESH:
-            timeout = settings.SESSION_TIMEOUT
-            token_life = request.user.token.expires - datetime.datetime.now(
-                datetime.timezone.utc)
-            session_time = min(timeout, int(token_life.total_seconds()))
-            request.session.set_expiry(session_time)
 
+        # NOTE: the AJAX check is intentionally BEFORE the session expiry
+        # refresh below, so background AJAX polling (auto-refreshing panels)
+        # does not keep resetting SESSION_TIMEOUT. The idle timeout must
+        # reflect genuine user activity (non-AJAX requests) only.
         if http_utils.is_ajax(request):
             # if the request is Ajax we do not want to proceed, as clients can
             #  1) create pages with constant polling, which can create race
@@ -83,6 +79,14 @@ class HorizonMiddleware(object):
             #  2) might leave a user seemingly left logged in forever
             #  3) thrashes db backed session engines with tons of changes
             return None
+        # Since we know the user is present and authenticated, lets refresh the
+        # session expiry if configured to do so.
+        if settings.SESSION_REFRESH:
+            timeout = settings.SESSION_TIMEOUT
+            token_life = request.user.token.expires - datetime.datetime.now(
+                datetime.timezone.utc)
+            session_time = min(timeout, int(token_life.total_seconds()))
+            request.session.set_expiry(session_time)
         # If we use cookie-based sessions, check that the cookie size does not
         # reach the max size accepted by common web browsers.
         if (
